WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.002 line:92%
-I'm delighted to join you.

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.771
-I was gonna say it's been an
interesting week in Washington.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel that has been true
for a long time.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:07.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is.
-Yeah.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
We are on a real streak of
interesting weeks.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
This week,
you had the president saying

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
that what was happening with
family separation

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:15.882 line:92%
was the Democrats' fault.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, the specifics of
the family separation,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was not true, it was
the Democrats' fault.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
But now, he signed
this executive order,

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.925 size:81% position:41%
which still allows for
indefinite detention

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.862
and does nothing to get these
children back to their families.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it now, with those problems
that have been created,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
is this a problem
for the president?

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.668
Or is this a problem for you
and your colleagues in Congress?

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:40.373
-Well, first of all, it's not
unusual for this president

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.609 line:92%
to blame others for problems

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:46.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he had
a big hand in creating.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:46.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.484
-And, so, just to be clear, he
created a policy a month ago,

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:55.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
back in May,
his zero-tolerance policy.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:01:00.393
And that policy resulted in what
we've just watched, aghast,

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:04.564
on our televisions and,
you know, in discussions.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.232 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's been heartbreaking.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
His executive order yesterday,
we're all waiting like,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.303 line:92%
"Oh, is he gonna reverse this?

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.505
Has he finally acknowledged that
this was immoral

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.841 size:84% position:42%
and that he needs to do
something about it?"

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.675 line:92%
And then we read the details.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:19.813
And, of course, it doesn't
address the over 2,000 children

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are already separated from
their parents.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:27.087
And it doesn't -- I mean,
it doesn't change the fact

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:31.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we would be jailing
children with their families,

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.258 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which is still wrong.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:35.862
And, you know, it's as though
the United States government

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
has just kidnapped
2,000 children

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:42.469
and there is no plan to reunite
them with their parents.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:45.171
And it's amazing that we're
talking about the idea that

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
we would need to have
Congress pass a bill to make

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
the administration
do the right thing here.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that may end up
being what we have to do.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:55.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With children being used as
political pawns --

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is something that
attorney general Jeff Sessions

00:01:58.551 --> 00:01:59.752 line:92%
basically admitted this is for.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
Chief of Staff John Kelly
admitted this was a deterrent,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.892
that if you take children
away from their parents,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.862 size:81% position:41% line:92%
less people will come.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:09.996 line:92%
Isn't it something -- you know,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.532
obviously, this is something
the administration is doing.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you surprised that
your Republican colleagues

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
aren't stepping forward faster
saying,

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.038
"Look, there's one thing
none of us should ever do,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.073 line:92%
no matter what our party is,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is to use children
as pawns"?

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.909
-Right.
But they haven't stepped forward

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.946
when it's happened in the past,
so this isn't the first time.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:30.617
Although this is probably,
you know, almost unspeakable

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
to watch children
being ripped away

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.287 line:92%
from their mothers and fathers.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:39.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
But whether it's for deterrent
effect, as they say,

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
or to get his wall.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He did this with Dreamers.
-Right.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:48.635
-And he did this with the child
health insurance program,

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:54.407
which was allowed to expire for
weeks and weeks and weeks.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:57.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're talking about children
getting the care

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.380
that they need
and not being dropped off of it.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.648 line:92%
So this is not the first time.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:06.920
And most of it has been
as leverage for his wall.

